# Anything not committed lives in one place.
local/

# Toolchain and editor leavings.
.venv/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.calibration-cache/
.env
.DS_Store

# What a run or a tool writes. An audit writes its results beside itself and this
# checkout is an obvious place to run one, so these are shapes rather than filenames:
# a new output should be covered on the day it is added, and two were not.
#
# Unanchored on purpose. The same names get written at three different depths, and a
# root-anchored pattern would leave the test that guards this green while the file it
# guards is committed one directory down.
# `tests/test_registry.py::AnAuditDoesNotCommitItself` reads the tools' own defaults,
# checks every one against `git check-ignore`, and carries the account of what went
# wrong before it existed.
checklist-results*
CHECKLIST*
*QUEUE*.md
probe-*.json
.seo-runs/
